<script>
import Code from '#src/lib/Code.abide'
import Doc from '#src/lib/Doc.abide'
import Example from '#src/lib/Example.abide'
import Section from '#src/lib/Section.abide'

import SizeToPanel from './lib/SizeToPanel.abide'
import sizeToPanel from './lib/SizeToPanel.abide' with { type: 'text' }
</script>

<Doc
    seeAlso={[
        '/behaviors/element-visible',
        '/behaviors/element-rect',
        '/headless/chart',
        '/abide-files/by-name',
    ]}
    tests={[
        {
            path: 'packages/abide/tests/element.test.ts',
            from: ["test('a delivery writes the value, and nothing before it does"],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/abide/tests/element.test.ts',
            from: [
                "test('given no target, host is spread and each field is a value of its own",
            ],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/abide/tests/element.test.ts',
            from: [
                "test('elementSize observes the box ResizeObserver names, and writes the device pixels it asks for",
            ],
        },
    ]}
>
    <Section level={3} title="Size a chart to its panel">
        <p>Call it with nothing and spread its <code>host</code> on the element, then read
            <code>width</code> and <code>height</code> by name. The browser writes them after
            each layout, and until the first one they are <code>undefined</code>.</p>
        <Example code={sizeToPanel}><SizeToPanel /></Example>
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Draw a canvas at the screen's own pixels">
        <p><code>box</code> takes the boxes <code>ResizeObserver</code> names.
            <code>'device-pixel-content-box'</code> writes the size in device pixels, so a
            canvas is as sharp as the screen.</p>
        <Code language="abide" caption="abide" code={`
            <script>
            import { elementSize } from '@abide/abide'

            const pixels = elementSize({ box: 'device-pixel-content-box' })
            </script>

            <canvas {...pixels.host} width={pixels.width} height={pixels.height}></canvas>
        `} />
    </Section>
</Doc>
